text During class...
text The English teacher keeps yapping incomprehensible things that sound like magical spells.
text I cannot understand a single word that reaches my ears.
text Though since I was never trying to listen to begin with, of course I wouldn't understand a thing.
text I glance in a different direction.
text Toward Fujibayashi.
text She's staring at the chalkboard with a serious look.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...Phew...
text I look back at my own desk.
text I am holding the letter that Kyou handed me this morning.
text I still haven't even opened it.
text Well, it is supposed to be from Fujibayashi, but... it feels really suspicious.
text ......
text In any case, guess I'll read it...
text I quietly peel off the cat sticker.
text I then take the letter out of the envelope.
text Its contents are really simple and easy to understand.
text It's just a single sentence written in round letters...
sound VY5.aac
text "I'll be waiting in the courtyard after school."
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text What a dodgy letter...
text It's so short, I have no idea whether it was really Fujibayashi who wrote this.
text In any case, its handwriting is different than the one on the front of the envelope.
text If the letter was just a little longer, then I'm sure Kyou would've messed up somewhere if she wrote this...
text I sigh, and once again look at Fujibayashi.
text ...She likes me, huh?
text It all feels somewhat surreal.
text It's true. You can really tell from the way Fujibayashi has been acting that her reaction hasn't been normal.
text But still, it would be really egotistical of me to simply write that off as her having a crush on me.
text Nevertheless...
text I am certain Kyou has her hand in this as well.
